  "title": "Number Names & Number Sense (3-Digit Numbers)",
  "emoji": "💯",
  "parentNote": "Say numbers out loud while writing them (\"Three hundred forty-five... 3, 4, 5\") — hearing and writing together builds the number-name skill fastest.",
  "learnBullets": [
    "Reading and writing **number names** for 3-digit numbers (e.g., 345 = Three Hundred Forty-Five)",
    "Finding numbers that come **before, after, and between**",
    "**Ascending** (small to big) and **Descending** (big to small) order",
    "Understanding **expanded form** (245 = 200 + 40 + 5)"
  ],
  "learnItFirst": "**Writing Number Names:**\n```\n345  →  Three Hundred Forty-Five\n100  →  One Hundred\n250  →  Two Hundred Fifty\n```\n\n**Expanded Form:** breaking a number into hundreds + tens + ones\n```\n345 = 300 + 40 + 5\n```\n\n**Before, After, Between:**\n```\n___ , 246 , ___     →   245 , 246 , 247\n(before)     (after)\n```\n\n### 🧠 How to Solve — 3 Easy Steps\n1. **Break** the number into hundreds, tens, and ones.\n2. **Say** each part's name in order (hundreds first, then tens-and-ones together).\n3. For before/after: **before** means subtract 1, **after** means add 1.\n\n---",
